---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';

// Target is roughly 400 words — something a person will actually finish.
// No skills list, no technology logos, no timeline widget.
const DESCRIPTION =
	'Founding CTO and employee #1 at AutogenAI, and twenty-five years delivering public services under government contract before that.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`About · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description={DESCRIPTION} />
		<style>
			main {
				width: 720px;
			}
			p {
				line-height: 1.65;
				margin-bottom: 1.1em;
			}
			.lead {
				font-size: 1.2rem;
				color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			<p class="lead">
				I build AI products for organisations that have to answer for how they work.
			</p>

			<p>
				I'm employee #1 and founding CTO at AutogenAI. Since July 2022 I've taken it from a blank
				repo to a category-defining product across three funding rounds — in production before
				ChatGPT existed — and built the organisation that runs it: a distributed team of 40
				spanning engineering, ML, product, platform, IT and GRC, across the UK, US and Australia.
			</p>

			<p>
				A good deal of that work was regulatory. We reached FedRAMP High authorisation in January
				2026, alongside SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001, Cyber Essentials Plus and IRAP. The harder part
				was architectural: keeping an AI system matched to a capability landscape that moved every
				six months, across four generations of models, with no rewrite event in four years.
			</p>

			<p>
				Before that I was CTO at Policy in Practice, a govtech business serving local authorities
				and central government — the same buyer, one technology generation earlier. And before
				software, twenty-five years delivering public services under government contract: designing
				and running government-funded employment programmes at Kennedy Scott, writing and winning
				the bids that paid for them, and founding Indus Delta, which grew into the sector's
				most-read community before I sold it to Inclusion in 2010.
			</p>

			<p>
				The convergence is the point. I spent years on the bidding side of government contracts,
				and I've spent the last four running frontier models in production for customers who have
				to account for the results. Those are not the same skill, and not many people have had to
				learn both.
			</p>

			<p>
				Along the way: a BSc in Mathematics from Warwick, an MSc in Computer Science from Birkbeck
				in 2022, a PGDip in Management Studies, and Makers Academy. Before any of it, two years
				teaching maths and physics in Central Africa with VSO — still the hardest job I have had.
			</p>

			<p>You can reach me at <a href="mailto:dan@whitston.uk">dan@whitston.uk</a>.</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
